menu "Modulus Tab5"

    config MODULUS_WIFI_ENABLED
        bool "Enable C6 hosted wireless (esp_hosted SDIO)"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, wireless_shim powers C6 via PI4IOE and brings up
            esp_wifi_remote over esp_hosted. Disable for P4-only bring-up.

    config MODULUS_C6_BOOT_DELAY_MS
        int "Delay (ms) after WLAN_PWR_EN before esp_hosted connect"
        depends on MODULUS_WIFI_ENABLED
        default 7000
        range 500 10000
        help
            Tab5 cold-boot: measure from first WLAN_PWR_EN (PI4IOE2 init in
            display_shim), WLAN_PWR cycle in wireless_shim, or last GPIO15
            reset (esp_hosted retry). C6 network_adapter needs ~3-5 s after
            power; esp_hosted GPIO15 reset inside esp_wifi_init reboots C6 —
            CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_SDIO_RESET_DELAY_MS must match this margin.
            Use 7000 ms on Tab5 (5500 ms esp_hosted delay + margin).
            Increase if sdmmc_card_init returns 0x107.
            Do NOT WLAN_PWR-cycle on ESP_RST_USB (serial monitor) — only ensure.

    config MODULUS_C6_THREAD_SUPPORTED
        bool "C6 OpenThread radio available (802.15.4 on SDIO ch10)"
        default n
        depends on MODULUS_WIFI_ENABLED
        help
            Default Modulus C6 image ships with Thread disabled. Enable only
            after flashing a C6 build with CONFIG_MODULUS_C6_THREAD=y.

    config MODULUS_ZIG_UI_ENGINE
        bool "Zig UI engine owns scanout (omit LVGL widget UI)"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, Core-0 zig_ui task drives MIPI via Zig Engine and
            the LVGL widget tree (ui_dashboard / ui_settings*) is not compiled.
            BSP still starts a thin LVGL port for panel bind. Set n for the
            legacy LVGL UI lab build.

endmenu
